From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 23:50:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Compact retained shaped text

A shaped paragraph keeps one Character per source character and one
ShapedCluster per cluster, so their size dominates retained text:

- Shaped text buffers drop their growth slack once shaping is done.
- A cluster stores only the start of its characters; its end comes from
  the next cluster or the shaped-text boundary.
- A character's grapheme start is a bit in its flags (Character 12 -> 8
  bytes on wasm32).
- Glyph and variation coordinate buffers are thin vectors, since most
  clusters have one inline glyph and most fonts no variations.
- Cluster and character positions come from a sparse index: a u32 base
  per 4096 clusters plus a u16 delta (ShapedCluster 16 -> 12 bytes,
  Character 8 -> 4 bytes), falling back to one base per cluster if a
  delta overflows.

Range access and shaping output are unchanged.

Signed-off-by: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
